WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.334
-Good evening, everybody.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.836
This is "Late Night."

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:05.204
We hope you're all doing well.

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:06.873
And now, let's get to the news.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:10.810
President Biden appeared
last night on an NBC special

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:14.614
celebrating Betty White and
then again on "Chicago Fire."

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.650
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.219
Former President Trump
reportedly told

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:22.254
his lawyer, Rudy Giuliani,
to ask

00:00:22.254 --> 00:00:23.856
the Department
of Homeland Security

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:26.859
if they could legally seize
voting machines

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:28.027
from swing states.

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:32.132
Said Trump, "Wrong.
I never said legally."

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:37.136
That's right, after losing
the election in 2020,

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:38.804
former President Trump
reportedly asked

00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:43.075
if Homeland Security could seize
voting machines in swing states.

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:46.179
And if you're wondering whether
or not that's evil,

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:49.916
let me point you to the word
"seize."

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:54.653
It's always evil when "seize"
is involved.

00:00:55.087 --> 00:00:56.856
For example, you will hear
a villain say,

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.024
"Seize them, you fools!"

00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:00.827
But you'll never, ever hear
anyone say,

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.595
"Hey, good news.
The mayor has seized

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.397
more funding for the arts."

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.467
It was reported yesterday that
some of

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:10.803
the Trump White House records
that were turned over

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:13.005
to the House committee
investigating the Capitol attack

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:15.708
had been ripped up
and taped back together.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:19.646
And from the looks of it,
so had some of the witnesses.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:22.982
Wow.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:25.685
"What happened, Steve?"
"Oh, I fell in the shredder."

00:01:28.487 --> 00:01:30.623
Former President Trump's
political team

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.927
announced yesterday that
he amassed over $120 million

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:36.095
in his war chest.
Or as he told the IRS,

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.231
$1.2 million.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:47.073
You know, I told the monologue
writers this morning --

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.975
I said, "Remember, tonight,

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:51.210
David Letterman's going to
be here."

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:57.283
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.519
"So bring --
bring your 'A' game."

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:07.026
And to a person, every single
one of them said,

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.596
"That's today?"

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:16.069
In a new interview,
New Jersey Governor Phil Murphy

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.569
said that the state needs to,
quote,

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:19.572
"learn to live with
the coronavirus pandemic,"

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:22.041
not to mention melanoma.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.180
"The New York Times" has
reportedly paid

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.282
in the low seven figures to
acquire

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.050
the daily word game, Wordle.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.719
But I got it in six.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:37.824
I was so happy.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:40.760
I'm doing Wordle jokes.
They finally started to work.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.530
[ Laughs ]

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:47.366
Producers have announced
a new prequel television series

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:49.168
based on the movie musical
"Grease"

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:51.671
that will take place four years
before the start of the film

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:54.908
when the students were still
in their early 30s.

00:02:57.409 --> 00:03:00.346
The national weather service in
Florida

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:03.182
warned over the weekend
that the cold temperatures

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:07.019
could immobilize iguanas,
calling them to fall out

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:08.454
of trees and appear dead.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:12.224
Experts added that residents
would only have a very limited

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:15.461
window to arrange them in funny
positions on their lawn.

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:23.169
I think we know they'd be
dirtier than that.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:29.107
And finally, Krispy Kreme
has released

00:03:29.107 --> 00:03:30.476
its Valentine's Day menu.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:33.713
It's the perfect way to
literally win someone's heart.

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.085
As our monologue writer,
Mike Scollins,

00:03:40.085 --> 00:03:41.587
who thought to himself,
you know,

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:44.089
the way to absolutely make
sure the last joke

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:47.961
in the monologue -- should note
that was the last one --

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:49.529
the way to make sure it lands
is end

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:52.231
with a picture of a man
in the hospital.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:55.634
That way even if you don't get
the joke --

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:58.471
[ Laughs ]

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:00.039
That was a monologue, everybody.

